The program is used to send Wake on LAN (WoL) frames over a local
Ethernet  network  to  one  or  more hosts using their link layer
(hardware) addresses.  WoL functionality is generally enabled  in
a  machine’s BIOS and can be used to power on machines from a re‐
mote system without having physical access to them.  is an Ether‐
net interface of the local machine and is used to send  the  Wake
on  LAN  frames  over  it.   If there is only one Ethernet device
available that is up and running, then the argument can be  omit‐
ted.   is the link layer address of the remote machine.  This can
be specified as a hardware address or as a hostname entry in  ac‐
cepts multiple addresses.  Link layer addresses can be determined
and  set  using  Ethernet host name data base.  The utility first
